### Goal Model Summary

#### Goals

| Name | Text | Runtime | Goal Type | Relation | Justification |
|------|------|---------|-----------|----------|---------------|
| G1   | Manage Food Delivery and Retrieval | - | Achieve | - | Ensures food delivery and retrieval are handled correctly. |
| G2   | Handle Food Delivery | - | Achieve | AND | Both delivery methods are necessary. |
| G3   | Handle Dish Retrieval | - | Achieve | AND | Both dish retrieval methods are necessary. |
| G2.1 | Direct Delivery | - | Achieve | OR | Alternative method for delivery. |
| G2.2 | Tray Retrieval | - | Achieve | OR | Alternative method for delivery. |
| G2.3 | Query Patient Ability | - | Query | AND | Necessary before proceeding with tray retrieval. |
| G3.1 | Unassisted Dish Retrieval | - | Achieve | OR | Alternative method for dish retrieval. |
| G3.2 | Assisted Dish Retrieval | - | Achieve | OR | Alternative method for dish retrieval. |
| G3.3 | Query Presence of Helper | - | Query | AND | Necessary before assisted retrieval. |
| G4   | Handle Door Opening | - | Achieve | AND | Necessary for delivery and retrieval. |
| G4.1 | Robot-Only Door Opening | - | Achieve | OR | Alternative method for door opening. |
| G4.2 | Human-Assisted Door Opening | - | Achieve | OR | Alternative method for door opening. |

#### Tasks

| Name | Text | Relation | Location | Number of Robots | Justification |
|------|------|----------|----------|------------------|---------------|
| AT1  | Deliver Food Directly | AND | Patient Room | 1 | Single robot delivers directly. |
| AT2  | Place Food on Tray | AND | Patient Room | 1 | Single robot places food. |
| AT3  | Retrieve Food from Tray | AND | Patient Room | 1 or 2 | May require cooperation. |
| AT4  | Check Patient Ability | AND | Hospital Database | 1 | Single robot queries data. |
| AT5  | Retrieve Dishes Unassisted | AND | Patient Room | 1 | Single robot retrieves dishes. |
| AT6  | Retrieve Dishes with Helper | AND | Patient Room | 1 or 2 | May require cooperation. |
| AT7  | Check Helper Presence | AND | Hospital Database | 1 | Single robot queries data. |
| AT8  | Open Door by Robot | AND | Patient Room | 1 | Single robot opens door. |
| AT9  | Open Door with Human | AND | Patient Room | 1 or 2 | May require human help. |

### Logical Relationships

- **G1 -> G2, G3 [AND]**  
  Justification: Both food delivery and dish retrieval are necessary for the mission.

- **G2 -> G2.1, G2.2 [OR]**  
  Justification: Either direct delivery or tray retrieval can fulfill food delivery.

- **G2.2 -> G2.3 [AND]**  
  Justification: Need to query patient ability before tray retrieval.

- **G3 -> G3.1, G3.2 [OR]**  
  Justification: Either unassisted or assisted dish retrieval can fulfill the goal.

- **G3.2 -> G3.3 [AND]**  
  Justification: Need to check for a helper before assisted retrieval.

- **G4 -> G4.1, G4.2 [OR]**  
  Justification: Either robot-only or human-assisted door opening can fulfill the goal.

### Explanation

The goal model is structured to ensure all aspects of food delivery and dish retrieval are covered, considering both autonomous and cooperative scenarios. Each goal is decomposed into sub-goals and tasks that reflect the necessary steps, ensuring the system can handle uncertainties and different cooperation needs.
